course: dictionary
lesson: 2811
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning fits. «He shouts that she is a common, low, fat barge-woman and that he is a well-known, distinguished Toad.» The words well-known are the clue: distinguished means famous and respected here.
explain: Distinguished can also describe someone who looks important and dignified, often an older person. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. If famous and respected does not fit, try looking important and dignified instead.
explain: Distinguish can also be a verb, meaning to see or show the difference between things. If you distinguished two birds by their beaks, you noticed how their beaks were different. The past form is distinguished, so the meaning depends on the sentence.
fact: Distinguished means famous and respected because of important work.
fact: «Distinguished» can also mean looking important and dignified, often an older person.
fact: Useful phrases include «distinguished guest», «distinguished career» and «distinguished from».
fact: As a verb, distinguish means to see or show the difference between things.
fact: Check the clue words around the word: well-known, important work or grey hair all point to a meaning.
exercise: «He shouts that she is a common, low, fat barge-woman and that he is a well-known, distinguished Toad.» What does distinguished mean here? | Cold and wet | *Famous and respected | Very small | Lost and confused
exercise: Lena says her grandad looks distinguished with his grey hair. What does distinguished suggest? | *Important, dignified and older-looking | Hungry | Lost and frightened | Very quick at running
exercise: «Ravi distinguished the oak leaves from the ash leaves.» What does distinguished mean in this sentence? | Lost track of | Painted over | *Saw the difference between | Ate
test: «The distinguished scientist won a prize for her important work.» What does distinguished mean? | Very frightened | *Famous and respected | Lost in a forest | Dirty and untidy
test: «Mia distinguished the twins by their freckles.» What does distinguished mean here? | Hid from | *Showed the difference between | Copied | Forgot about
exam: Read: «He shouts that she is a common, low, fat barge-woman and that he is a well-known, distinguished Toad.» Which word is the clue that distinguished means famous? | barge-woman | common | shouts | *well-known
